1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
This looks painted — not one stroke is paint.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Every color here is crushed glass.

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,400
It starts as a bare copper body.

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,800
Flat copper wire is bent by hand.

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,000
Thousands of tiny cells, no glue.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,400
Each cell is filled with enamel paste.

8
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,800
Double-tap if you'd hold this one.

9
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,400
Fired in a kiln, glass melts to color.

10
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,000
Six centuries on, they call it Jingtai Blue.

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
★ Expert Tip: Buy from a workshop kiln, not a tourist stall.

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,600
Follow your China Travel Expert — one China secret daily.
